From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:51:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 22/62] mobile: a tap after a two-finger touch that moved is a
 tap again

DoubleFinerTapGestureRecognizer remembers that a first finger landed
(_isStart) and which fingers lifted (_upTap) until its timer runs out, which
the two-finger tap patch raised to 500 ms. When a two-finger touch turned
into something else, for example the first finger lifted and the second
dragged the cursor, the arena rejected the recognizer, but _reject reset that
state only through _firstTap, which this recognizer never sets. The next
finger down within the 500 ms counted as the second finger of the old touch
and its lift as the second lift: a single tap right-clicked in mouse mode and
was lost in touch mode. 1.5.0 had the same flaw within its 300 ms window.

The recognizer now forgets the touch once it tracks none of its fingers. A
test replays the reported case: the tap 250 ms after the drag is a tap, not a
two-finger tap.

(Release 1.5.1 review, dart-behavior finding 2.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 flutter/lib/common/widgets/gestures.dart |  7 +++++++
 flutter/test/mobile_gestures_test.dart   | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/flutter/lib/common/widgets/gestures.dart b/flutter/lib/common/widgets/gestures.dart
index 61348f6..72dd5c0 100644
--- a/flutter/lib/common/widgets/gestures.dart
+++ b/flutter/lib/common/widgets/gestures.dart
@@ -607,6 +607,13 @@ class DoubleFinerTapGestureRecognizer extends GestureRecognizer {
     _trackers.remove(tracker.pointer);
     tracker.entry.resolve(GestureDisposition.rejected);
     _freezeTracker(tracker);
+    if (_trackers.isEmpty) {
+      // No finger of this touch is left to tap (it moved, or another gesture
+      // won it): the next finger down is a first finger again.
+      _stopFirstTapUpTimer();
+      _isStart = false;
+      _upTap.clear();
+    }
     if (_firstTap != null) {
       if (tracker == _firstTap) {
         _reset();
diff --git a/flutter/test/mobile_gestures_test.dart b/flutter/test/mobile_gestures_test.dart
index dddb45d..5349688 100644
--- a/flutter/test/mobile_gestures_test.dart
+++ b/flutter/test/mobile_gestures_test.dart
@@ -92,4 +92,24 @@ void main() {
     }, log: [], holdTapMove: false);
     expect(log, ['tap@60']);
   });
+
+  testWidgets('a tap after a two-finger touch that moved is a tap', (t) async {
+    final log = await _run(t, (now) async {
+      final a = await t.startGesture(const Offset(100, 100), pointer: 1);
+      final b = await t.startGesture(const Offset(150, 100), pointer: 2);
+      await t.pump(const Duration(milliseconds: 40));
+      await a.up();
+      for (var i = 0; i < 20; i++) {
+        await b.moveBy(const Offset(3, 0));
+        await t.pump(const Duration(milliseconds: 8));
+      }
+      await b.up();
+      // Within the two-finger tap's 500 ms window.
+      await t.pump(const Duration(milliseconds: 250));
+      final c = await t.startGesture(const Offset(300, 300), pointer: 3);
+      await t.pump(const Duration(milliseconds: 40));
+      await c.up();
+    }, log: []);
+    expect(log.where((e) => !e.startsWith('panStart')), ['tap@790']);
+  });
 }
